# Student Management System (Java OOP Project)

📌 Project Overview
The Student Management System is a Java-based console application developed to manage basic information about students and teachers.  

This project demonstrates core Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts such as inheritance and method overriding.

🎯 Purpose of the Project
- To apply Object-Oriented Programming in a real project
- To understand class relationships in Java
- To practice inheritance and method overriding
- To manage simple data for students and teachers

🧱 Project Structure (Classes)

1. Person.java
- Parent class for the system
- Contains common attributes like name and ID

2. Student.java
- Inherits from Person
- Represents student-related information

3. Teacher.java
- Inherits from Person
- Demonstrates method overriding and teacher-specific behavior

4. StudentManagement.java
- Handles system operations
- Manages students and teachers in the system

5. Main.java
- Entry point of the program
- Runs the application

---

⚙️ OOP Concepts Used
- Inheritance (Student and Teacher extend Person)
- Method Overriding
- Encapsulation
- Class interaction and structure

---

🚀 How to Run
1. Open project in a Java IDE (VS Code / IntelliJ / Eclipse)
2. Compile all .java files
3. Run Main.java
4. View output in the console
## 📌 Note
This project was created as part of a Student Management System assignment to demonstrate basic Java programming and OOP principles.
